/* docker: "Explained step by step" walkthroughs. */

explain('d1',`
<p>"But it works on my machine!" is the most famous excuse in software. Docker exists to kill it: you ship the app <b>and</b> everything it needs as one sealed package that runs the same everywhere.</p>

${V.card(1,'Works on my machine','the problem Docker solves',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 214" role="img" aria-label="Without a container the app works on the laptop with Node 24 but breaks on a server with Node 18. Packed in a container with its own Node 24, it works on both"><text class="t-b" x="10" y="22" style="font-size:15px">Without Docker</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="32" width="190" height="74" rx="8"/>${V.ic('laptop',14,40,56,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-m" x="78" y="62" style="font-size:15px">app</text><text class="t-m" x="78" y="86" style="font-size:15px">Node 24</text>${V.ic('check',150,48,36,'ic-ok')}<rect class="bx-bad" x="224" y="32" width="190" height="74" rx="8"/>${V.ic('server',232,40,56,'ic-bad')}<text class="t-m" x="296" y="62" style="font-size:15px">app</text><text class="t-m" x="296" y="86" style="font-size:15px">Node 18</text>${V.ic('cross',368,48,36,'ic-bad')}<text class="t-b" x="10" y="132" style="font-size:15px">With Docker</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="142" width="190" height="66" rx="8"/>${V.ic('laptop',14,148,52,'ic-ok')}<rect class="bx-a" x="72" y="152" width="112" height="46" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="128" y="179.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">app+Node 24</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="224" y="142" width="190" height="66" rx="8"/>${V.ic('server',232,148,52,'ic-ok')}<rect class="bx-a" x="290" y="152" width="112" height="46" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="346" y="179.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">app+Node 24</text></svg><figcaption>Top: the same code behaves differently because the machines differ. Bottom: the app travels inside a container that brings its own Node, so every machine runs the identical package.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>Shipping containers. Before the 1950s, every ship was loaded by hand with sacks and barrels of every shape. Then came one standard steel box: cranes, ships and lorries don't care what is inside, they just move the box. Docker does the same for software.</p>`)}
${V.why(`<p>Apps depend on things around them: the language version, system libraries, settings. Those differ between your laptop, a teammate's laptop and the server, so bugs appear "only in production". Docker (2013) made Linux's built-in isolation features easy to use: put the app and its whole environment in one box.</p>`)}
${V.hook(`Ship the whole kitchen, not just the recipe.`)}
`)}

${V.card(2,'Images and containers','the template and the running copy',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 196" role="img" aria-label="One image, like a cookie cutter, makes three identical containers"><rect class="bx-info" x="6" y="40" width="130" height="110" rx="8"/>${V.ic('jar',38,50,64,'ic-info')}<text class="t-b" x="71" y="134" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">image</text><path class="ln-a" d="M136 95H170M170 40V150M170 40H190M170 95H190M170 150H190"/><rect class="bx-ok" x="196" y="18" width="150" height="44" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',204,22,36,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-m" x="250" y="46" style="font-size:14px">container 1</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="196" y="73" width="150" height="44" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',204,77,36,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-m" x="250" y="101" style="font-size:14px">container 2</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="196" y="128" width="150" height="44" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',204,132,36,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-m" x="250" y="156" style="font-size:14px">container 3</text><text class="t t-ok" x="380" y="62" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">run</text><text class="t t-ok" x="380" y="82" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">many</text><text class="t" x="71" y="176" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">read-only template</text><text class="t" x="270" y="190" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">running copies</text></svg><figcaption>An <b>image</b> is the frozen package: files plus the command to start. A <b>container</b> is one running copy of it. You can start as many containers from one image as you like.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>A cake recipe and the cakes. The recipe (the <b>image</b>) never changes; each cake you bake from it (a <b>container</b>) is a separate thing you can eat, decorate or throw away. If you code: an image is a class, a container is an object.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'docker'],' ',[2,'run'],' ',[3,'hello-world']],[
 '<b>docker.</b> The command-line tool that talks to the Docker Engine.',
 '<b>run.</b> Create a new container from an image and start it. Pulls the image first if you don\'t have it.',
 '<b>Image name.</b> With no tag, Docker adds <code>:latest</code>, so this is <code>hello-world:latest</code>.'])}
<p><b>Watch what one docker run really does.</b></p>
${V.steps([
 ['You type <b>docker run hello-world</b>. Docker first looks on your own machine for an image with that name. There isn\'t one.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 252" role="img" aria-label="Docker cannot find the image locally"><rect class="bx" x="6" y="8" width="190" height="70" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="16" y="28" style="font-size:14px">your images</text>${V.ic('jar',18,34,38,'ic-info')}<text class="t-m t-dim" x="64" y="62" style="font-size:15px">(none)</text><rect class="bx" x="224" y="8" width="190" height="70" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="234" y="28" style="font-size:14px">Docker Hub</text>${V.ic('cloud',236,32,42,'ic-info')}<text class="t-m" x="286" y="62" style="font-size:14px">hello-world</text><rect class="ln-d" x="6" y="90" width="408" height="56" rx="8"/><text class="t t-dim" x="210" y="123" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">no container yet</text><rect class="bx-dark" x="6" y="156" width="408" height="88" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="180" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">$ docker run hello-world</text><text class="t-term t-warn" x="16" y="202" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">Unable to find image 'hello-world:latest'</text><text class="t-term t-warn" x="16" y="224" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">  locally</text></svg>`],
 ['So it downloads (<b>pulls</b>) the image from Docker Hub, the public library of images. It is now stored on your machine for next time.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 252" role="img" aria-label="Docker pulls the image from Docker Hub"><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="8" width="190" height="70" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="16" y="28" style="font-size:14px">your images</text>${V.ic('jar',18,34,38,'ic-info')}<text class="t-m" x="64" y="62" style="font-size:15px">hello-world</text><rect class="bx-hl" x="224" y="8" width="190" height="70" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="234" y="28" style="font-size:14px">Docker Hub</text>${V.ic('cloud',236,32,42,'ic-info')}<text class="t-m" x="286" y="62" style="font-size:14px">hello-world</text><path class="ln-a" d="M222 50H206"/><polygon class="ah-a" points="208,43 208,57 198,50"/><rect class="ln-d" x="6" y="90" width="408" height="56" rx="8"/><text class="t t-dim" x="210" y="123" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">no container yet</text><rect class="bx-dark" x="6" y="156" width="408" height="88" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="180" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">latest: Pulling from library/hello-world</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="202" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">Status: Downloaded newer image for</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="224" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">  hello-world:latest</text></svg>`],
 ['Docker creates a <b>container</b> from the image and starts its one main program.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 252" role="img" aria-label="A container is created and starts"><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="8" width="190" height="70" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="16" y="28" style="font-size:14px">your images</text>${V.ic('jar',18,34,38,'ic-info')}<text class="t-m" x="64" y="62" style="font-size:15px">hello-world</text><rect class="bx" x="224" y="8" width="190" height="70" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="234" y="28" style="font-size:14px">Docker Hub</text>${V.ic('cloud',236,32,42,'ic-info')}<text class="t-m" x="286" y="62" style="font-size:14px">hello-world</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="90" width="408" height="56" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',16,96,44,'ic-a')}<text class="t-m" x="72" y="116" style="font-size:15px">container from hello-world</text><text class="t-b" x="72" y="136" style="font-size:14px">running</text><rect class="bx-dark" x="6" y="156" width="408" height="88" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="180" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">creating container...</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="202" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">starting the main process</text></svg>`],
 ['The program prints its message...',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 252" role="img" aria-label="The container prints Hello from Docker"><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="8" width="190" height="70" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="16" y="28" style="font-size:14px">your images</text>${V.ic('jar',18,34,38,'ic-info')}<text class="t-m" x="64" y="62" style="font-size:15px">hello-world</text><rect class="bx" x="224" y="8" width="190" height="70" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="234" y="28" style="font-size:14px">Docker Hub</text>${V.ic('cloud',236,32,42,'ic-info')}<text class="t-m" x="286" y="62" style="font-size:14px">hello-world</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="90" width="408" height="56" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',16,96,44,'ic-a')}<text class="t-m" x="72" y="116" style="font-size:15px">container from hello-world</text><text class="t-b" x="72" y="136" style="font-size:14px">running</text><rect class="bx-dark" x="6" y="156" width="408" height="88" rx="8"/><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="180" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">Hello from Docker!</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="202" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">This message shows that your installation</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="224" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">appears to be working correctly.</text></svg>`],
 ['...and finishes. A container only lives as long as its main program, so it stops. <b>docker ps -a</b> lists it as <b>Exited (0)</b>: 0 means "finished with no error".',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 252" role="img" aria-label="The container has exited with code 0"><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="8" width="190" height="70" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="16" y="28" style="font-size:14px">your images</text>${V.ic('jar',18,34,38,'ic-info')}<text class="t-m" x="64" y="62" style="font-size:15px">hello-world</text><rect class="bx" x="224" y="8" width="190" height="70" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="234" y="28" style="font-size:14px">Docker Hub</text>${V.ic('cloud',236,32,42,'ic-info')}<text class="t-m" x="286" y="62" style="font-size:14px">hello-world</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="90" width="408" height="56" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',16,96,44,'ic-a')}<text class="t-m" x="72" y="116" style="font-size:15px">container from hello-world</text><text class="t-b" x="72" y="136" style="font-size:14px">Exited (0)</text><rect class="bx-dark" x="6" y="156" width="408" height="88" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="180" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">$ docker ps -a</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="202" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">IMAGE        STATUS</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="224" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">hello-world  Exited (0) 5 seconds ago</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.ok('docker ps','Lists running containers only'),V.ok('docker ps -a','All containers, including stopped (Exited) ones'),
 V.no('"my container crashed"','Exited (0) is not a crash. The main program simply finished'),V.ok('docker --version','Check Docker is installed'))}
${V.hook(`Image: the recipe. Container: the cake. A container lives exactly as long as its main program.`)}
`)}

${V.card(3,'Containers vs virtual machines','why containers are so light',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 232" role="img" aria-label="Virtual machines each carry a whole guest operating system. Containers share the host kernel, so they are much smaller and faster"><text class="t-b" x="103" y="20" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">Virtual machines</text><rect class="bx-a" x="6" y="30" width="94.0" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t" x="53" y="49.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">App A</text><rect class="bx-a" x="106.0" y="30" width="94.0" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t" x="153" y="49.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">App B</text><rect class="bx-warn" x="6" y="64" width="94.0" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t" x="53" y="83.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">Guest OS</text><rect class="bx-warn" x="106.0" y="64" width="94.0" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t" x="153" y="83.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">Guest OS</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="98" width="194" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t" x="103" y="117.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">Hypervisor</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="132" width="194" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t" x="103" y="151.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">Host OS</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="166" width="194" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t" x="103" y="185.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">Hardware</text><text class="t-b t-a" x="103" y="216" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">GBs, minutes to boot</text><text class="t-b" x="317" y="20" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">Containers</text><rect class="bx-a" x="220" y="30" width="94.0" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t" x="267" y="49.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">App A</text><rect class="bx-a" x="320.0" y="30" width="94.0" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t" x="367" y="49.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">App B</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="220" y="64" width="94.0" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t" x="267" y="83.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">libs</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="320.0" y="64" width="94.0" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t" x="367" y="83.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">libs</text><rect class="bx" x="220" y="98" width="194" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t" x="317" y="117.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">Docker Engine</text><rect class="bx" x="220" y="132" width="194" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t" x="317" y="151.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">Host OS (shared kernel)</text><rect class="bx" x="220" y="166" width="194" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t" x="317" y="185.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">Hardware</text><text class="t-b t-a" x="317" y="216" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">MBs, seconds to start</text></svg><figcaption>A virtual machine pretends to be a whole computer, with its own full operating system inside. A container shares the host's kernel (the core of the OS) and only packs what the app needs.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>A virtual machine is a whole detached house: its own walls, plumbing and heating. A container is a flat in a block: private front door, but the building's foundations and pipes are shared. Flats are far cheaper and quicker to move into.</p>`)}
${V.why(`<p>Virtual machines isolate well but are heavy: each one carries a full operating system. Containers isolate the app using features of the Linux kernel itself, so there is nothing extra to boot. That is why you can run dozens on a laptop.</p>`)}
${V.rules(V.ok('one main process','A container is built around one main program'),V.no('a container is a tiny VM','It has no kernel of its own; it shares the host\'s'))}
${V.build(`<ol><li>Check Docker is installed with <code>docker --version</code>.</li><li>Run the <code>hello-world</code> image and read its message.</li><li>List all containers, stopped ones included, and find the Exited status.</li></ol>`)}
${V.hook(`A VM is a house; a container is a flat sharing the same foundations.`)}
`)}

<div class="try"><b>Try it in your head</b>1. You run one image three times. How many containers? <i>Three.</i> 2. Why does hello-world show Exited? <i>Its main program finished.</i> 3. What does a container share with the host? <i>The kernel.</i></div>
`);

explain('d2',`
<p>Time to run a real web server in one line. To use it you need three ideas: where images come from, how a container's door (its port) connects to your machine, and how to stop and tidy up afterwards.</p>

${V.card(1,'Pulling images','download once, run many times',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 196" role="img" aria-label="Docker Hub holds many images with tags. docker pull copies nginx:latest onto your machine"><rect class="bx-info" x="6" y="8" width="200" height="180" rx="8"/>${V.ic('cloud',16,14,40,'ic-info')}<text class="t-b" x="64" y="40" style="font-size:15px">Docker Hub</text><rect class="bx-a" x="16" y="58" width="180" height="34" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="106" y="80.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">nginx:latest</text><rect class="bx" x="16" y="100" width="180" height="34" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="106" y="122.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">nginx:alpine</text><rect class="bx" x="16" y="142" width="180" height="34" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="106" y="164.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">postgres:16</text><path class="ln-a" d="M206 75H254"/><polygon class="ah-a" points="252,68 252,82 262,75"/><text class="t-m t-a" x="234" y="64" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700">pull</text><rect class="bx" x="262" y="8" width="152" height="180" rx="8"/>${V.ic('laptop',306,14,64,'ic-a')}<text class="t-b" x="338" y="98" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">your images</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="272" y="112" width="132" height="34" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="338" y="133.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">nginx:latest</text><text class="t" x="338" y="172" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">188 MB, kept</text></svg><figcaption>An image lives in a <b>registry</b> such as Docker Hub. <code>docker pull</code> downloads a copy; <code>docker images</code> lists what you have. After that, starting containers needs no internet.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>An app store. Docker Hub is the store, an image is the app, and <code>docker pull</code> is pressing "download". Tags are like version numbers on the download button.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'docker pull'],' ',[2,'nginx'],[3,':'],[4,'latest']],[
 '<b>docker pull.</b> Download an image from a registry.',
 '<b>Repository.</b> The image\'s name. Official images like <code>nginx</code> and <code>postgres</code> need no username.',
 '<b>Colon.</b> Separates the name from the tag.',
 '<b>Tag.</b> Which version. Leave it out and you get <code>latest</code>, which just means "the default tag", not always the newest.'])}
${V.rules(V.ok('postgres:16','Pin a version so it can\'t change under you'),V.ok('nginx:alpine','Variant tags: alpine builds are much smaller'),V.ok('docker images','List the images you have'))}
${V.hook(`name:tag. No tag means <code>:latest</code>.`)}
`)}

${V.card(2,'Running with ports','a street door into the container',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 150" role="img" aria-label="Your machine is a block of flats. Port 8080 on the street door leads to flat 80 inside the container"><rect class="bx" x="6" y="10" width="408" height="130" rx="8"/>${V.ic('house',16,20,48,'ic-info')}<text class="t-b" x="72" y="48" style="font-size:15px">your machine</text><rect class="bx-warn" x="6" y="70" width="70" height="46" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="41" y="98.95" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700">8080</text><path class="ln-a" d="M76 93H192"/><polygon class="ah-a" points="190,86 190,100 200,93"/><text class="t-m t-a" x="138" y="84" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">-p 8080:80</text><rect class="bx-a" x="200" y="52" width="204" height="78" rx="8"/>${V.ic('door',210,62,40,'ic-a')}<rect class="bx-ok" x="254" y="70" width="50" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="279" y="95.95" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700">80</text><text class="t-m" x="356" y="96" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700">nginx</text></svg><figcaption>A container is a flat with no door to the street. <code>-p 8080:80</code> fits a street door numbered 8080 that leads straight to the flat's door 80. Left side = your machine, right side = the container.</figcaption></figure>
${V.why(`<p>Containers are isolated on purpose: nothing outside can reach them unless you say so. Publishing a port is you saying so, one door at a time, which keeps everything else safely shut.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'docker run'],' ',[2,'-d'],' ',[3,'-p 8080'],[4,':80'],' ',[5,'--name web'],' ',[6,'nginx']],[
 '<b>docker run.</b> Create and start a container.',
 '<b>-d (detached).</b> Run in the background and give your terminal back.',
 '<b>Host port.</b> The door on YOUR machine. Always on the left.',
 '<b>Container port.</b> The door inside the container that the app listens on. nginx uses 80.',
 '<b>--name.</b> A name you choose, so you don\'t have to use a random one.',
 '<b>Image.</b> Always last, after all the options.'])}
<p><b>Follow one request</b> from curl to nginx and back.</p>
${V.steps([
 ['You ask your own machine for <b>localhost:8080</b>. The request arrives at port 8080, a numbered door on your computer.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 210" role="img" aria-label="The request reaches port 8080 on your machine"><rect class="bx-a" x="4" y="40" width="100" height="96" rx="8"/>${V.ic('laptop',24,48,60,'ic-a')}<text class="t-m" x="54" y="126" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">curl</text><rect class="bx" x="128" y="8" width="288" height="162" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="140" y="30" style="font-size:14px">your machine</text><rect class="bx-hl" x="120" y="66" width="58" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="149" y="93.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">8080</text><rect class="bx" x="236" y="40" width="170" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',246,46,34,'ic-a')}<text class="t-b" x="288" y="68" style="font-size:14px">container</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="226" y="88" width="48" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="250" y="113.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">80</text><text class="t-m" x="340" y="116" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700">nginx</text><path class="ln-a" d="M104 88H112"/><polygon class="ah-a" points="110,81 110,95 120,88"/><text class="t-b t-a" x="210" y="198" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">request arrives at port 8080</text></svg>`],
 ['Because you ran with <b>-p 8080:80</b>, Docker watches door 8080 and passes everything through to door <b>80</b> inside the container.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 210" role="img" aria-label="Docker forwards port 8080 to container port 80"><rect class="bx-a" x="4" y="40" width="100" height="96" rx="8"/>${V.ic('laptop',24,48,60,'ic-a')}<text class="t-m" x="54" y="126" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">curl</text><rect class="bx" x="128" y="8" width="288" height="162" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="140" y="30" style="font-size:14px">your machine</text><rect class="bx-hl" x="120" y="66" width="58" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="149" y="93.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">8080</text><rect class="bx-a" x="236" y="40" width="170" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',246,46,34,'ic-a')}<text class="t-b" x="288" y="68" style="font-size:14px">container</text><rect class="bx-hl" x="226" y="88" width="48" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="250" y="113.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">80</text><text class="t-m" x="340" y="116" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700">nginx</text><path class="ln-a" d="M178 88H218"/><polygon class="ah-a" points="216,81 216,95 226,88"/><text class="t-m t-a" x="202" y="152" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">-p</text><text class="t-b t-a" x="210" y="198" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">Docker forwards 8080 to 80</text></svg>`],
 ['nginx, listening on port 80 inside its container, receives the request and builds the reply.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 210" role="img" aria-label="nginx inside the container answers"><rect class="bx-a" x="4" y="40" width="100" height="96" rx="8"/>${V.ic('laptop',24,48,60,'ic-a')}<text class="t-m" x="54" y="126" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">curl</text><rect class="bx" x="128" y="8" width="288" height="162" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="140" y="30" style="font-size:14px">your machine</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="120" y="66" width="58" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="149" y="93.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">8080</text><rect class="bx-a" x="236" y="40" width="170" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',246,46,34,'ic-a')}<text class="t-b" x="288" y="68" style="font-size:14px">container</text><rect class="bx-hl" x="226" y="88" width="48" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="250" y="113.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">80</text><text class="t-m" x="340" y="116" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700">nginx</text><circle class="dot-ok" cx="340" cy="138" r="7"/><text class="t-b t-a" x="210" y="198" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">nginx builds the page</text></svg>`],
 ['The reply travels back the same way, and curl prints the nginx welcome page.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 210" role="img" aria-label="The reply returns to curl"><rect class="bx-a" x="4" y="40" width="100" height="96" rx="8"/>${V.ic('laptop',24,48,60,'ic-a')}<text class="t-m" x="54" y="126" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">curl</text><rect class="bx" x="128" y="8" width="288" height="162" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="140" y="30" style="font-size:14px">your machine</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="120" y="66" width="58" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="149" y="93.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">8080</text><rect class="bx-a" x="236" y="40" width="170" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',246,46,34,'ic-a')}<text class="t-b" x="288" y="68" style="font-size:14px">container</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="226" y="88" width="48" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="250" y="113.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">80</text><text class="t-m" x="340" y="116" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700">nginx</text><path class="ln-ok" d="M226 140H112"/><polygon class="ah-ok" points="114,133 114,147 104,140"/><text class="t-b t-ok" x="210" y="198" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">Welcome to nginx!</text></svg>`],
 ['Without <b>-p</b>, nothing is waiting at 8080. The container is sealed off, so curl gets "connection refused" even though nginx is running fine.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 210" role="img" aria-label="Without -p the connection is refused"><rect class="bx-a" x="4" y="40" width="100" height="96" rx="8"/>${V.ic('laptop',24,48,60,'ic-a')}<text class="t-m" x="54" y="126" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">curl</text><rect class="bx" x="128" y="8" width="288" height="162" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="140" y="30" style="font-size:14px">your machine</text><rect class="bx-bad" x="120" y="66" width="58" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="149" y="93.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">8080</text><rect class="bx" x="236" y="40" width="170" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',246,46,34,'ic-a')}<text class="t-b" x="288" y="68" style="font-size:14px">container</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="226" y="88" width="48" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="250" y="113.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">80</text><text class="t-m" x="340" y="116" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700">nginx</text><text class="t-b t-bad" x="210" y="198" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">Connection refused: no -p</text><path class="ln" d="M104 88H112"/><polygon class="ah" points="110,81 110,95 120,88"/></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.rh('Rules'),
 V.ok('-p 8080:80','HOST:CONTAINER. Read it as "my 8080 goes to its 80"'),V.no('-p 80:8080','Backwards: nginx is not listening on 8080 inside'),
 V.no('docker run nginx -d','Options after the image name are passed to the app, not to Docker'),
 V.no('port is already allocated','Something already uses that host port. Pick another, like 8081'))}
${V.hook(`Left is my machine, right is the container. <code>-p</code> is the street door.`)}
`)}

${V.card(3,'Life of a container','run, look, stop, remove',`
${V.like(`<p>Hiring a van. You pick it up (run), check the dashboard (logs), park it with the engine off (stop), and return it (rm). The van company (the image) still has the model for next time.</p>`)}
${V.steps([
 ['<b>docker run -d</b> starts web in the background and prints its long ID. <b>docker ps</b> shows it <b>Up</b>.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 186" role="img" aria-label="web is up"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="174" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">$ docker run -d -p 8080:80 --name web nginx</text><text class="t-term t-dim" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">3f9c1e7a52b0...</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">$ docker ps</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">NAMES  STATUS         PORTS</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="156" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">web    Up 5 seconds   0.0.0.0:8080-&gt;80/tcp</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>docker logs web</b> shows what nginx has printed, including the request you just made.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 156" role="img" aria-label="docker logs shows the request"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="144" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ docker logs web</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">172.17.0.1 - - "GET / HTTP/1.1" 200</text><text class="t-term t-dim" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">(one line per request)</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>docker stop web</b> asks nginx to shut down. The container still exists, just <b>Exited</b>. You could start it again.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 156" role="img" aria-label="web has exited"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="144" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ docker stop web</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ docker ps -a</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">NAMES  STATUS</text><text class="t-term t-warn" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">web    Exited (0) 2 seconds ago</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>docker rm web</b> deletes the stopped container. Now the name web is free to use again. The nginx image is still on your machine.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 156" role="img" aria-label="web is removed"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="144" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ docker rm web</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ docker ps -a</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">NAMES  STATUS</text><text class="t-term t-dim" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">(empty)</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.no('docker rm web (while running)','Refused. Stop it first, or use docker rm -f web'),V.no('--name web (twice)','"name already in use": remove the old one first'),
 V.ok('docker logs -f web','Follow the logs live, like tail -f'))}
${V.build(`<ol><li>Pull the nginx image and list your images.</li><li>Run it in the background, named, with your port 8080 published to its port 80.</li><li>Ask for the page with <code>curl localhost:8080</code>.</li><li>Read the container's logs.</li><li>Stop it, then remove it.</li></ol>`)}
${V.hook(`run, ps, logs, stop, rm: start it, see it, hear it, park it, return it.`)}
`)}

<div class="try"><b>Try it in your head</b>1. <code>-p 5000:80</code>: which address in your browser? <i>localhost:5000.</i> 2. Can you remove a running container with plain <code>docker rm</code>? <i>No: stop it first or add -f.</i> 3. What tag does <code>docker pull redis</code> fetch? <i>latest.</i></div>
`);

explain('d3',`
<p>Pulling other people's images is useful; packaging <b>your own</b> app is the real superpower. A Dockerfile is a short recipe, and once you have one, anyone can build and run your app with two commands.</p>

${V.card(1,'The Dockerfile','a recipe, one instruction per line',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="An image is a stack of layers, one per instruction, with node:24-alpine at the bottom and your code on top"><rect class="bx-a" x="20" y="196" width="300" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="170" y="217.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">FROM node:24-alpine</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="26" y="158" width="288" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="170" y="179.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">WORKDIR /app</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="32" y="120" width="276" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="170" y="141.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">COPY package*.json ./</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="38" y="82" width="264" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="170" y="103.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">RUN npm install</text><rect class="bx-warn" x="44" y="44" width="252" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="170" y="65.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">COPY . .</text><text class="t t-a" x="340" y="214" style="font-size:14px">base</text><text class="t t-ok" x="340" y="100" style="font-size:14px">deps</text><text class="t t-warn" x="340" y="62" style="font-size:14px">your code</text><text class="t-m" x="10" y="22" style="font-size:15px">CMD ["node","server.js"]</text><text class="t t-a" x="410" y="22" text-anchor="end" style="font-size:14px">start note</text></svg><figcaption>Each instruction adds one layer on top of the last, like a stack of trays. The bottom is a ready-made <b>base image</b>; your code goes on top. CMD adds no files: it just records what to run at start.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>Building a sandwich in layers. Bread first (the base image), then butter (a working folder), then the filling (your packages), then the topping (your code). The written recipe card is the Dockerfile.</p>`)}
${V.why(`<p>Typing install steps by hand on every server is slow and easy to get wrong. A Dockerfile writes them down once, in a file that lives next to your code, so the image is rebuilt exactly the same way every time.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'FROM'],' node:24-alpine\n',[2,'WORKDIR'],' /app\n',[3,'COPY'],' package*.json ./\n',[4,'RUN'],' npm install\n',[3,'COPY'],' . .\n',[5,'EXPOSE'],' 3000\n',[6,'CMD'],' ["node", "server.js"]'],[
 '<b>FROM.</b> The base image to start from: Node 24 on Alpine, a tiny Linux. Always the first line.',
 '<b>WORKDIR.</b> The folder inside the image where everything happens. Created if missing.',
 '<b>COPY.</b> Copy files from your project (left) into the image (right). <code>package*.json</code> matches package.json and package-lock.json.',
 '<b>RUN.</b> Run a command <b>while building</b>, and save the result as a layer.',
 '<b>EXPOSE.</b> A note saying which port the app uses. It does not publish it; that is still <code>-p</code>.',
 '<b>CMD.</b> The command to run <b>when a container starts</b>.'])}
${V.rules(V.rh('Rules'),
 V.ok('CMD ["node", "server.js"]','JSON form: double quotes, commas, square brackets'),V.no("CMD ['node', 'server.js']",'Single quotes aren\'t valid JSON, so Docker treats it as a plain shell string'),
 V.no('RUN node server.js','RUN happens at build time. The server would start and the build would never finish'),
 V.rh('Conventions'),V.ok('.dockerignore','List node_modules and .env in it so they are never copied in'),V.ok('-alpine, -slim','Small base images build and download faster'))}
${V.hook(`RUN is for building, CMD is for starting.`)}
`)}

${V.card(2,'Building and the layer cache','why the order of lines matters',`
${V.anat([[1,'docker build'],' ',[2,'-t hello-api'],' ',[3,'.']],[
 '<b>docker build.</b> Read a Dockerfile and produce an image.',
 '<b>-t (tag).</b> The name for the new image. Lower case only.',
 '<b>Build context.</b> The folder whose files COPY can see. The dot means "this folder". Easy to forget!'])}
<p><b>Watch the cache work.</b> Blue layers are reused, yellow ones are rebuilt.</p>
${V.steps([
 ['First build. Docker runs each instruction in order and saves the result as a layer. <b>RUN npm install</b> is the slow one: it downloads every package.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="First build in progress"><text class="t-b" x="10" y="24" style="font-size:15px">docker build -t hello-api .</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="410" y="24" text-anchor="end" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">...</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="40" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="16" y="62" style="font-size:15px">FROM node:24-alpine</text><text class="t-b t-ok" x="306" y="62" style="font-size:15px">built</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="78" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="16" y="100" style="font-size:15px">WORKDIR /app</text><text class="t-b t-ok" x="306" y="100" style="font-size:15px">built</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="116" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="16" y="138" style="font-size:15px">COPY package*.json ./</text><text class="t-b t-ok" x="306" y="138" style="font-size:15px">built</text><rect class="bx-hl" x="6" y="154" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="16" y="176" style="font-size:15px">RUN npm install</text><text class="t-b" x="306" y="176" style="font-size:15px">running...</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="192" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m t-dim" x="16" y="214" style="font-size:15px">COPY . .</text><text class="t-b" x="306" y="214" style="font-size:15px"></text></svg>`],
 ['All five layers built and stacked into the image <b>hello-api</b>.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="First build done"><text class="t-b" x="10" y="24" style="font-size:15px">docker build -t hello-api .</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="410" y="24" text-anchor="end" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">45 s</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="40" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="16" y="62" style="font-size:15px">FROM node:24-alpine</text><text class="t-b t-ok" x="306" y="62" style="font-size:15px">built</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="78" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="16" y="100" style="font-size:15px">WORKDIR /app</text><text class="t-b t-ok" x="306" y="100" style="font-size:15px">built</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="116" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="16" y="138" style="font-size:15px">COPY package*.json ./</text><text class="t-b t-ok" x="306" y="138" style="font-size:15px">built</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="154" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="16" y="176" style="font-size:15px">RUN npm install</text><text class="t-b t-ok" x="306" y="176" style="font-size:15px">built</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="192" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="16" y="214" style="font-size:15px">COPY . .</text><text class="t-b t-ok" x="306" y="214" style="font-size:15px">built</text></svg>`],
 ['You change one line in <b>server.js</b> and build again. Docker checks each layer\'s inputs. The first four didn\'t change, so they are reused: <b>CACHED</b>. Only COPY . . (your code) is redone.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="Rebuild reuses four cached layers"><text class="t-b" x="10" y="24" style="font-size:15px">after editing server.js</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="410" y="24" text-anchor="end" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">2 s</text><rect class="bx-info" x="6" y="40" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="16" y="62" style="font-size:15px">FROM node:24-alpine</text><text class="t-b t-info" x="306" y="62" style="font-size:15px">CACHED</text><rect class="bx-info" x="6" y="78" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="16" y="100" style="font-size:15px">WORKDIR /app</text><text class="t-b t-info" x="306" y="100" style="font-size:15px">CACHED</text><rect class="bx-info" x="6" y="116" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="16" y="138" style="font-size:15px">COPY package*.json ./</text><text class="t-b t-info" x="306" y="138" style="font-size:15px">CACHED</text><rect class="bx-info" x="6" y="154" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="16" y="176" style="font-size:15px">RUN npm install</text><text class="t-b t-info" x="306" y="176" style="font-size:15px">CACHED</text><rect class="bx-warn" x="6" y="192" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="16" y="214" style="font-size:15px">COPY . .</text><text class="t-b t-warn" x="306" y="214" style="font-size:15px">rebuilt</text></svg>`],
 ['Why the order matters: if <b>COPY . .</b> came before <b>npm install</b>, every code edit would change that layer, and every layer after it, including the slow install, would rebuild too.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="With COPY . . first, every edit reruns npm install"><text class="t-b t-bad" x="10" y="24" style="font-size:15px">bad order</text><text class="t-m t-bad" x="410" y="24" text-anchor="end" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">45 s</text><rect class="bx-info" x="6" y="40" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="151" y="61.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">FROM node:24-alpine</text><text class="t-b t-info" x="306" y="62" style="font-size:15px">CACHED</text><rect class="bx-info" x="6" y="78" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="151" y="99.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">WORKDIR /app</text><text class="t-b t-info" x="306" y="100" style="font-size:15px">CACHED</text><rect class="bx-warn" x="6" y="116" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="151" y="137.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">COPY . .</text><text class="t-b t-warn" x="306" y="138" style="font-size:15px">changed</text><rect class="bx-bad" x="6" y="154" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="151" y="175.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">RUN npm install</text><text class="t-b t-bad" x="306" y="176" style="font-size:15px">rebuilt!</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="192" width="290" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="151" y="213.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">...</text><text class="t-b" x="306" y="214" style="font-size:15px"></text></svg>`]])}
${V.like(`<p>Re-doing homework. If only the last question changed, you copy your earlier answers and redo just that one. But Docker is strict: once one layer changes, every layer above it must be redone too.</p>`)}
${V.rules(V.ok('COPY package*.json, RUN npm install, then COPY . .','Things that change rarely go first'),V.no('docker build -t hello-api','Missing the final dot: "requires 1 argument"'))}
${V.hook(`Slow and stable at the bottom, fast-changing code at the top.`)}
`)}

${V.card(3,'From Dockerfile to running app','build, run, curl',`
${V.steps([
 ['<b>docker build</b> turns the Dockerfile into an image. <b>-t</b> gives it a name; the final <b>.</b> says "the files are in this folder".',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 156" role="img" aria-label="docker build names the image hello-api"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="144" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ docker build -t hello-api .</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre"> => [5/5] COPY . .</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre"> => naming to hello-api</text></svg>`],
 ['Start a container from your own image, exactly as you did with nginx.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 156" role="img" aria-label="docker run starts the api container"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="144" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ docker run -d -p 3000:3000 \\</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">    --name api hello-api</text><text class="t-term t-dim" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">8b21c0f4e9d3...</text></svg>`],
 ['CMD runs <b>node server.js</b> inside the container, and the app answers on port 3000.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 150" role="img" aria-label="curl gets Hello from Docker"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="138" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ curl localhost:3000</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">Hello from Docker</text></svg>`]])}
${V.build(`<ol><li>Open a new Dockerfile in nano.</li><li>Start FROM a Node 24 Alpine image and set WORKDIR to /app.</li><li>Copy only the package files, run npm install, then copy everything else.</li><li>EXPOSE 3000 and set CMD to start server.js.</li><li>Build it with a name and the dot, run it with port 3000 published, and curl it.</li><li>Edit the message in server.js, rebuild, and spot the CACHED lines.</li></ol>`)}
${V.hook(`Dockerfile, build, run: recipe, cake tin, cake.`)}
`)}

<div class="try"><b>Try it in your head</b>1. Which instruction runs at container start? <i>CMD.</i> 2. You edit server.js. Does npm install rerun? <i>No, if the package files are copied and installed before COPY . .</i> 3. What does the final dot in docker build mean? <i>Use this folder as the build context.</i></div>
`);

explain('d4',`
<p>Containers are meant to be thrown away and replaced. That raises three questions every real app must answer: where do the settings come from, where does the data live, and how do containers talk to each other?</p>

${V.card(1,'Environment variables','settings from outside the image',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 190" role="img" aria-label="One postgres image runs as three containers, each given different environment variables for laptop, test and production"><rect class="bx-info" x="125" y="6" width="170" height="58" rx="8"/>${V.ic('jar',135,12,44,'ic-info')}<text class="t-m" x="186" y="42" style="font-size:15px">postgres:16</text><path class="ln-a" d="M210 64V80H70V96M210 80V96M210 80H350V96"/><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="96" width="130" height="84" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',14,102,30,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-b" x="50" y="122" style="font-size:14px">laptop</text><text class="t-m" x="16" y="148" style="font-size:14px">PASSWORD=</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="16" y="170" style="font-size:14px">secret</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="145" y="96" width="130" height="84" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',153,102,30,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-b" x="189" y="122" style="font-size:14px">test</text><text class="t-m" x="155" y="148" style="font-size:14px">PASSWORD=</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="155" y="170" style="font-size:14px">t3st!</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="284" y="96" width="130" height="84" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',292,102,30,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-b" x="328" y="122" style="font-size:14px">production</text><text class="t-m" x="294" y="148" style="font-size:14px">PASSWORD=</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="294" y="170" style="font-size:14px">long+random</text></svg><figcaption>The image stays the same everywhere. Each container gets its own settings from <b>environment variables</b> passed with <code>-e</code>, so one image serves your laptop, testing and the real site.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>A hotel room key card. Every card is the same kind of card, but each is programmed with a different room number at the desk. The image is the blank card; <code>-e</code> programs it.</p>`)}
${V.why(`<p>If settings like passwords were baked into the image, you would need a different image for each place, and your secrets would travel with it. Passing them in at start keeps one image for everywhere.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'-e'],' ',[2,'POSTGRES_PASSWORD'],[3,'='],[4,'secret']],[
 '<b>-e (environment).</b> Set one variable. Repeat <code>-e</code> for more.',
 '<b>Name.</b> Each image documents which names it reads. Capitals by convention.',
 '<b>Equals.</b> No spaces around it.',
 '<b>Value.</b> Quote it if it has spaces or symbols.'])}
<p><b>A classic first mistake</b>, made on purpose so you learn to read logs.</p>
${V.steps([
 ['Start Postgres without a password. <b>docker run</b> prints an ID and seems fine...',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 150" role="img" aria-label="db seems to start"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="138" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ docker run -d --name db postgres:16</text><text class="t-term t-dim" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">a71d02c95e3f...</text></svg>`],
 ['...but <b>docker ps -a</b> shows it already stopped with exit code <b>1</b>, meaning an error.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 150" role="img" aria-label="db exited with code 1"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="138" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ docker ps -a</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">NAMES  STATUS</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">db     Exited (1) 3 seconds ago</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>docker logs db</b> shows the program\'s last words. It even tells you the fix.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 186" role="img" aria-label="logs explain the missing password"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="174" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ docker logs db</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">Error: Database is uninitialized and</text><text class="t-term t-bad" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">superuser password is not specified.</text><text class="t-term t-warn" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">You must specify POSTGRES_PASSWORD</text><text class="t-term t-warn" x="16" y="156" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">to a non-empty value...</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.ok('docker logs NAME','The first thing to run when a container won\'t stay up'),V.no('-e POSTGRES_PASSWORD = secret','No spaces around ='),
 V.no('ENV PASSWORD=... in a Dockerfile','Secrets baked into an image leak with it'))}
${V.hook(`Same image everywhere; settings come in through <code>-e</code>.`)}
`)}

${V.card(2,'Volumes','data that outlives the container',`
${V.like(`<p>A hotel room and a storage locker. The room (container) is cleaned out when you check out. The locker (volume) belongs to you and stays put, ready for your next stay.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'-v'],' ',[2,'pgdata'],[3,':'],[4,'/var/lib/postgresql/data']],[
 '<b>-v (volume).</b> Attach storage to the container.',
 '<b>Volume name.</b> Docker creates it if it doesn\'t exist yet (or make it first with <code>docker volume create pgdata</code>).',
 '<b>Colon.</b> Outside on the left, inside on the right, just like <code>-p</code>.',
 '<b>Path inside.</b> Where the app writes its data. For Postgres it is this exact folder.'])}
${V.steps([
 ['Run Postgres with <b>-v pgdata:/var/lib/postgresql/data</b>. The folder where Postgres keeps its files is now really stored in the volume <b>pgdata</b>, outside the container.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 210" role="img" aria-label="The container folder is connected to the pgdata volume"><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="20" width="220" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',16,28,36,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-b" x="60" y="50" style="font-size:14px">db (container 1)</text><text class="t-m" x="18" y="80" style="font-size:14px">/var/lib/</text><text class="t-m" x="18" y="100" style="font-size:14px">postgresql/data</text><path class="ln" d="M166 92H272"/><polygon class="ah" points="270,85 270,99 280,92"/><rect class="bx-warn" x="280" y="20" width="134" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('db',300,28,44,'ic-warn')}<text class="t-m" x="347" y="94" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px;font-weight:700">pgdata</text><rect class="bx-dark" x="6" y="154" width="408" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="182" style="font-size:15px">-v pgdata:/var/lib/postgresql/data</text></svg>`],
 ['You create a <b>users</b> table. Postgres writes it into its data folder, which means into the volume.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 210" role="img" aria-label="The users table is stored in the volume"><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="20" width="220" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',16,28,36,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-b" x="60" y="50" style="font-size:14px">db (container 1)</text><text class="t-m" x="18" y="80" style="font-size:14px">/var/lib/</text><text class="t-m" x="18" y="100" style="font-size:14px">postgresql/data</text><path class="ln-a" d="M166 92H272"/><polygon class="ah-a" points="270,85 270,99 280,92"/><rect class="bx-warn" x="280" y="20" width="134" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('db',300,28,44,'ic-warn')}<text class="t-m" x="347" y="94" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px;font-weight:700">pgdata</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="292" y="104" width="110" height="28" rx="8"/><text class="t" x="347" y="122.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">users table</text><rect class="bx-dark" x="6" y="154" width="408" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="182" style="font-size:15px">psql: CREATE TABLE users ...</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>docker rm -f db</b> deletes the container and everything inside it. But the volume was never inside it, so <b>pgdata</b> and the table survive.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 210" role="img" aria-label="The container is gone, the volume remains"><rect class="ln-d" x="6" y="20" width="220" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('cross',90,50,48,'ic-bad')}<text class="t t-bad" x="116" y="124" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">removed</text><rect class="bx-warn" x="280" y="20" width="134" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('db',300,28,44,'ic-warn')}<text class="t-m" x="347" y="94" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px;font-weight:700">pgdata</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="292" y="104" width="110" height="28" rx="8"/><text class="t" x="347" y="122.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">users table</text><rect class="bx-dark" x="6" y="154" width="408" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="182" style="font-size:15px">$ docker rm -f db</text></svg>`],
 ['Start a new container on the same volume. Postgres finds existing data and says <b>Skipping initialization</b>. Your table is back.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 210" role="img" aria-label="A new container uses the same volume and finds the data"><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="20" width="220" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',16,28,36,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-b" x="60" y="50" style="font-size:14px">db (container 2)</text><text class="t-m" x="18" y="80" style="font-size:14px">/var/lib/</text><text class="t-m" x="18" y="100" style="font-size:14px">postgresql/data</text><path class="ln-a" d="M166 92H272"/><polygon class="ah-a" points="270,85 270,99 280,92"/><rect class="bx-warn" x="280" y="20" width="134" height="120" rx="8"/>${V.ic('db',300,28,44,'ic-warn')}<text class="t-m" x="347" y="94" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px;font-weight:700">pgdata</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="292" y="104" width="110" height="28" rx="8"/><text class="t" x="347" y="122.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">users table</text><rect class="bx-dark" x="6" y="154" width="408" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="182" style="font-size:15px">Skipping initialization: data found</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.ok('docker volume ls','List your volumes'),V.no('database without -v','Remove the container and every row is gone for good'),
 V.no('docker volume rm pgdata','Deletes the data itself. Only when you really mean it'))}
${V.hook(`Containers are rooms; volumes are lockers. Lock your data in the locker.`)}
`)}

${V.card(3,'Networks and exec','talking by name, and stepping inside',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 176" role="img" aria-label="On the network appnet, the api container reaches the database simply by the name db"><rect class="ln-d" x="6" y="8" width="408" height="160" rx="16"/><text class="t-b t-a" x="20" y="32" style="font-size:15px">network: appnet</text><rect class="bx-a" x="24" y="56" width="140" height="90" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',34,64,36,'ic-a')}<text class="t-m" x="94" y="130" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700">api</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="256" y="56" width="140" height="90" rx="8"/>${V.ic('db',266,64,36,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-m" x="326" y="130" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700">db</text><path class="ln-a" d="M164 100H248"/><polygon class="ah-a" points="246,93 246,107 256,100"/><text class="t-m t-a" x="210" y="90" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">db:5432</text></svg><figcaption>Containers on the same user-made network can find each other by <b>container name</b>. Docker runs a tiny phone book (DNS) that turns the name <code>db</code> into the right address.</figcaption></figure>
${V.why(`<p>Container IP addresses change every time a container is recreated, so typing them would break constantly. Names don't change. Docker's own default network can't look up names, which is why you create your own with <code>docker network create</code> and join it with <code>--network</code>.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'docker exec'],' ',[2,'-it'],' ',[3,'db'],' ',[4,'psql -U postgres']],[
 '<b>docker exec.</b> Run an extra command inside a container that is already running.',
 '<b>-it.</b> Interactive with a terminal, so you can type into it.',
 '<b>Container.</b> Which one.',
 '<b>Command.</b> Here the Postgres shell, logged in as the user postgres. Type <code>\\q</code> to leave.'])}
${V.rules(V.ok('--network appnet','Put every container that must talk on the same network'),V.ok('db:5432','Reach a container by its name and its inside port'),
 V.no('localhost:5432','From inside a container, localhost is that container itself'))}
${V.build(`<ol><li>Create a network and a volume.</li><li>Start Postgres with no password, see it exit, and read why in its logs.</li><li>Remove it and start it again with a password, the network and the volume.</li><li>Open psql inside it with <code>docker exec -it</code>.</li><li>Force-remove the container, start a fresh one on the same volume, and check the logs for "Skipping initialization".</li></ol>`)}
${V.hook(`<code>-e</code> settings, <code>-v</code> data, <code>--network</code> friends.`)}
`)}

<div class="try"><b>Try it in your head</b>1. You <code>docker rm</code> a database container that used <code>-v</code>. Is the data gone? <i>No, it is in the volume.</i> 2. A container keeps exiting. First command? <i>docker logs NAME.</i> 3. How does the api reach Postgres on appnet? <i>By its name: db:5432.</i></div>
`);

explain('d5',`
<p>A real app is a team of containers: your code, a database, maybe a cache. Starting each one by hand with long commands is a recipe for typos. Docker Compose writes the whole team down in one file and starts it with one command.</p>

${V.card(1,'compose.yaml','the whole app in one file',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" role="img" aria-label="One compose.yaml file describes the web and db services and the pgdata volume; one command starts them all"><rect class="bx-info" x="6" y="10" width="150" height="180" rx="8"/>${V.ic('file',14,20,32,'ic-info')}<text class="t-m" x="48" y="42" style="font-size:14px">compose.yaml</text><text class="t-m" x="20" y="80" style="font-size:14px">services:</text><text class="t-m t-a" x="34" y="104" style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700">web:</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="34" y="128" style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700">db:</text><text class="t-m" x="20" y="156" style="font-size:14px">volumes:</text><text class="t-m t-warn" x="34" y="178" style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700">pgdata:</text><path class="ln-a" d="M156 100H188"/><polygon class="ah-a" points="186,93 186,107 196,100"/><text class="t-m t-a" x="176" y="90" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700">up</text><rect class="ln-d" x="196" y="10" width="218" height="180" rx="12"/><text class="t" x="206" y="32" style="font-size:14px">shop_default network</text><rect class="bx-a" x="210" y="46" width="90" height="70" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',222,52,30,'ic-a')}<text class="t-m" x="255" y="104" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px;font-weight:700">web</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="314" y="46" width="90" height="70" rx="8"/>${V.ic('db',326,52,30,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-m" x="359" y="104" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px;font-weight:700">db</text><rect class="bx-warn" x="262" y="134" width="100" height="46" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="312" y="162.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">pgdata</text><path class="ln-d" d="M359 116V134"/></svg><figcaption>Instead of typing long docker run commands, you describe the whole app once. <code>docker compose up</code> reads the file and creates the network, the volume and every container.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>Sheet music for an orchestra. Instead of shouting instructions at each player, the conductor hands out one score. Everyone reads it and plays together. <code>compose.yaml</code> is the score; each service is a player.</p>`)}
${V.why(`<p>Teams kept writing shell scripts full of docker run commands. Compose (which grew out of a 2013 tool called Fig) replaced them with one readable file you can commit next to your code, so every developer starts exactly the same stack.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'services:'],'\n  ',[2,'web:'],'\n    build: .\n    ',[3,'ports:'],' ["3000:3000"]\n    ',[4,'environment:'],'\n      DATABASE_URL: postgres://...@db:5432/shop\n    ',[5,'depends_on:'],' [db]\n  ',[2,'db:'],'\n    ',[6,'image:'],' postgres:16'],[
 '<b>services.</b> The list of containers that make up the app.',
 '<b>Service name.</b> You choose it, and it becomes the hostname other services use.',
 '<b>ports.</b> Same as <code>-p</code>: HOST:CONTAINER.',
 '<b>environment.</b> Same as <code>-e</code>, one per line.',
 '<b>depends_on.</b> Start db before web. It only sets the order; it doesn\'t wait until the database is ready.',
 '<b>image or build.</b> Use a ready-made image, or <code>build: .</code> to build from your Dockerfile.'])}
${V.rules(V.rh('Rules: YAML is strict about spaces'),
 V.ok('two spaces per level','Indentation shows what belongs to what'),V.no('tabs','YAML refuses tab characters'),
 V.ok('"3000:3000"','Quote port pairs so YAML can\'t misread them as numbers'))}
${V.hook(`One file, one command, the whole band plays.`)}
`)}

${V.card(2,'up and down','start and stop the whole stack',`
${V.anat([[1,'docker compose'],' ',[2,'up'],' ',[3,'-d']],[
 '<b>docker compose.</b> Reads compose.yaml in this folder. (Old tutorials write <code>docker-compose</code> with a hyphen; that is the retired version 1.)',
 '<b>up.</b> Create and start everything. Run it again after editing the file and it updates only what changed.',
 '<b>-d.</b> Detached: in the background.'])}
${V.steps([
 ['<b>web</b> has <code>build: .</code>, so Compose first builds its image from the Dockerfile in this folder.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="web image built"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="32" style="font-size:15px">$ docker compose up -d</text><rect class="bx-hl" x="6" y="56" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="77" style="font-size:15px">image</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="77" style="font-size:15px">built web</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="92" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="113" style="font-size:15px">network</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="113" style="font-size:15px"></text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="128" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="149" style="font-size:15px">volume</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="149" style="font-size:15px"></text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="164" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="185" style="font-size:15px">db</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="185" style="font-size:15px"></text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="200" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="221" style="font-size:15px">web</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="221" style="font-size:15px"></text></svg>`],
 ['Then it creates a private <b>network</b> for this app, named after the folder: shop_default.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="Network created"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="32" style="font-size:15px">$ docker compose up -d</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="56" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="77" style="font-size:15px">image</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="77" style="font-size:15px">built web</text><rect class="bx-hl" x="6" y="92" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="113" style="font-size:15px">network</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="113" style="font-size:15px">shop_default</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="128" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="149" style="font-size:15px">volume</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="149" style="font-size:15px"></text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="164" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="185" style="font-size:15px">db</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="185" style="font-size:15px"></text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="200" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="221" style="font-size:15px">web</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="221" style="font-size:15px"></text></svg>`],
 ['Then the named <b>volume</b> for the database, also prefixed with the folder name.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="Volume created"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="32" style="font-size:15px">$ docker compose up -d</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="56" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="77" style="font-size:15px">image</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="77" style="font-size:15px">built web</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="92" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="113" style="font-size:15px">network</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="113" style="font-size:15px">shop_default</text><rect class="bx-hl" x="6" y="128" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="149" style="font-size:15px">volume</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="149" style="font-size:15px">shop_pgdata</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="164" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="185" style="font-size:15px">db</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="185" style="font-size:15px"></text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="200" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="221" style="font-size:15px">web</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="221" style="font-size:15px"></text></svg>`],
 ['<b>db</b> starts first, because web <b>depends_on</b> it...',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="db started"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="32" style="font-size:15px">$ docker compose up -d</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="56" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="77" style="font-size:15px">image</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="77" style="font-size:15px">built web</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="92" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="113" style="font-size:15px">network</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="113" style="font-size:15px">shop_default</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="128" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="149" style="font-size:15px">volume</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="149" style="font-size:15px">shop_pgdata</text><rect class="bx-hl" x="6" y="164" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="185" style="font-size:15px">db</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="185" style="font-size:15px">started</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="200" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="221" style="font-size:15px">web</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="221" style="font-size:15px"></text></svg>`],
 ['...then <b>web</b>. One command, the whole app running in the background.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="all started"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="32" style="font-size:15px">$ docker compose up -d</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="56" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="77" style="font-size:15px">image</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="77" style="font-size:15px">built web</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="92" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="113" style="font-size:15px">network</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="113" style="font-size:15px">shop_default</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="128" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="149" style="font-size:15px">volume</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="149" style="font-size:15px">shop_pgdata</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="164" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="185" style="font-size:15px">db</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="185" style="font-size:15px">started</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="200" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="221" style="font-size:15px">web</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="221" style="font-size:15px">started</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>docker compose down</b> removes the containers and the network. The volume is kept, so the data survives. (<code>down -v</code> would delete it too.)',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 236" role="img" aria-label="compose down keeps the volume"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="32" style="font-size:15px">$ docker compose down</text><rect class="bx" x="6" y="56" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="77" style="font-size:15px">image</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="77" style="font-size:15px">kept</text><rect class="bx-bad" x="6" y="92" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="113" style="font-size:15px">network</text><text class="t-m t-bad" x="140" y="113" style="font-size:15px">removed</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="128" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="149" style="font-size:15px">volume</text><text class="t-m" x="140" y="149" style="font-size:15px">kept</text><rect class="bx-bad" x="6" y="164" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="185" style="font-size:15px">db</text><text class="t-m t-bad" x="140" y="185" style="font-size:15px">removed</text><rect class="bx-bad" x="6" y="200" width="408" height="30" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="18" y="221" style="font-size:15px">web</text><text class="t-m t-bad" x="140" y="221" style="font-size:15px">removed</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.ok('docker compose ps','The status of this app\'s containers'),V.ok('docker compose logs web','Logs of one service. Add -f to follow'),
 V.no('docker compose down -v','Also deletes the volumes, and your data with them'))}
${V.hook(`up builds the stage, down clears it, the volume stays in the wings.`)}
`)}

${V.card(3,'The localhost trap','talk to services by name',`
${V.like(`<p>Every container is its own house. Saying "localhost" inside a container is like saying "my house". If the database lives next door, you have to use its address: its service name.</p>`)}
${V.steps([
 ['The app is told to find Postgres at <b>localhost:5432</b>. But inside a container, <b>localhost</b> means "this container". web looks inside itself, finds no database, and the connection is refused.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 206" role="img" aria-label="localhost points back into web itself"><rect class="bx-a" x="6" y="20" width="170" height="110" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',16,28,34,'ic-a')}<text class="t-m" x="60" y="52" style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700">web</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="244" y="20" width="170" height="110" rx="8"/>${V.ic('db',254,28,34,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-m" x="298" y="52" style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700">db</text><text class="t-m" x="258" y="100" style="font-size:14px">:5432 open</text><text class="t-m t-bad" x="18" y="88" style="font-size:15px">localhost:5432</text><path class="ln-a" d="M120 100C150 140 40 150 60 106"/><polygon class="ah-a" points="52,110 62,98 68,112"/><rect class="bx-bad" x="6" y="148" width="408" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="210" y="176" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1:5432</text></svg>`],
 ['Fix: use the <b>service name</b>. On the Compose network, the name <b>db</b> turns into the database container\'s address.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 206" role="img" aria-label="db resolves to the db container"><rect class="bx-a" x="6" y="20" width="170" height="110" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',16,28,34,'ic-a')}<text class="t-m" x="60" y="52" style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700">web</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="244" y="20" width="170" height="110" rx="8"/>${V.ic('db',254,28,34,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-m" x="298" y="52" style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700">db</text><text class="t-m" x="258" y="100" style="font-size:14px">:5432 open</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="18" y="88" style="font-size:15px">db:5432</text><path class="ln-ok" d="M176 75H236"/><polygon class="ah-ok" points="234,68 234,82 244,75"/><rect class="bx-info" x="6" y="148" width="408" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t" x="210" y="176" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px">Compose DNS: "db" is that container</text></svg>`],
 ['After <code>docker compose up -d</code> again, web connects. Same code, one word changed in the settings.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 206" role="img" aria-label="web connects to Postgres"><rect class="bx-a" x="6" y="20" width="170" height="110" rx="8"/>${V.ic('container',16,28,34,'ic-a')}<text class="t-m" x="60" y="52" style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700">web</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="244" y="20" width="170" height="110" rx="8"/>${V.ic('db',254,28,34,'ic-ok')}<text class="t-m" x="298" y="52" style="font-size:17px;font-weight:700">db</text><text class="t-m" x="258" y="100" style="font-size:14px">:5432 open</text><text class="t-m t-ok" x="18" y="88" style="font-size:15px">db:5432</text><path class="ln-ok" d="M176 75H236"/><polygon class="ah-ok" points="234,68 234,82 244,75"/><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="148" width="408" height="44" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="210" y="176" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">Connected to Postgres at db:5432</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.no('@localhost:5432','Inside web, this is web itself'),V.ok('@db:5432','The service name, on the shared Compose network'),
 V.ok('localhost:3000 from your laptop','Fine: on your own machine you reach the published port'))}
${V.build(`<ol><li>Read the provided compose.yaml and spot the two services and the volume.</li><li>Start the stack in the background.</li><li>curl the API and read the connection error.</li><li>Change the database host in DATABASE_URL from localhost to the service name, then run up again.</li><li>curl again, check <code>docker compose ps</code>, then bring everything down.</li></ol>`)}
${V.hook(`In a container, localhost is me. Everyone else has a name.`)}
`)}

<div class="try"><b>Try it in your head</b>1. Which command stops and removes the whole stack? <i>docker compose down.</i> 2. web needs Postgres. Which host goes in its URL? <i>db, the service name.</i> 3. Does depends_on wait until the database accepts connections? <i>No, it only controls start order.</i></div>
`);

explain('d6',`
<p>You have built an image; now it has to leave your laptop and reach a server. Two habits make that fast and safe: ship only what is needed, and give every release a clear name and version.</p>

${V.card(1,'Multi-stage builds','build in the workshop, ship from the shop',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 206" role="img" aria-label="A big workshop image with Node and tools builds the site; only the finished dist folder is carried into a small nginx shop image"><rect class="bx-warn" x="6" y="10" width="180" height="130" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="16" y="32" style="font-size:15px">workshop: build</text>${V.ic('gear',18,44,40,'ic-warn')}${V.ic('terminal',64,44,40,'ic-warn')}${V.ic('box',110,44,40,'ic-warn')}<text class="t" x="16" y="118" style="font-size:14px">Node + npm</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="110" y="96" width="66" height="34" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="143" y="118.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">dist</text><path class="ln-ok" d="M176 113H244"/><polygon class="ah-ok" points="242,106 242,120 252,113"/><text class="t-m t-ok" x="214" y="104" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">COPY</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="252" y="40" width="162" height="100" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="262" y="62" style="font-size:14px">shop: nginx:alpine</text>${V.ic('house',268,72,40,'ic-ok')}<rect class="bx-ok" x="318" y="84" width="66" height="34" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="351" y="106.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">dist</text><rect class="bx-bad" x="6" y="156" width="300" height="18" rx="4"/><text class="t-m" x="312" y="170" style="font-size:14px">site:fat</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="6" y="182" width="16" height="18" rx="4"/><text class="t-m" x="30" y="196" style="font-size:14px">site:slim</text></svg><figcaption>The first stage is a workshop full of tools. The last stage is the shop: it receives only the finished goods (the dist folder). The bars show the difference in image size, over 1 GB against under 100 MB.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>A bakery. The kitchen has ovens, mixers and flour everywhere. The shop window only shows the finished cakes. Customers never need the ovens, so you don't put them in the window.</p>`)}
${V.why(`<p>To build a frontend you need Node and hundreds of packages. To serve it you need only the output files and a web server. Shipping the tools wastes download time and space, and every extra program is one more thing an attacker could exploit.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'FROM node:24-alpine AS build'],'\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY package*.json ./\nRUN npm install\nCOPY . .\n',[2,'RUN npm run build'],'\n\n',[3,'FROM nginx:alpine'],'\n',[4,'COPY --from=build'],' ',[5,'/app/dist'],' ',[6,'/usr/share/nginx/html']],[
 '<b>Stage 1 with a name.</b> <code>AS build</code> lets a later stage refer to it.',
 '<b>The build.</b> Creates the dist folder of finished files.',
 '<b>Stage 2.</b> A second FROM starts fresh. The last stage is the image you get.',
 '<b>--from=build.</b> Copy from the named stage instead of from your project folder.',
 '<b>Source.</b> The path inside stage 1.',
 '<b>Destination.</b> Where nginx looks for web pages.'])}
${V.steps([
 ['Stage 1 starts from a Node image and is named <b>build</b> with <b>AS build</b>. It has everything needed to compile the site.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 220" role="img" aria-label="Stage 1 starts from node"><rect class="bx-warn" x="6" y="8" width="196" height="150" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="16" y="30" style="font-size:15px">stage 1: build</text><text class="t-m" x="16" y="54" style="font-size:14px">node:24-alpine</text><rect class="bx-dark" x="6" y="170" width="408" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="196" style="font-size:15px">FROM node:24-alpine AS build</text></svg>`],
 ['It installs packages and runs the build, producing a <b>dist/</b> folder: plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 220" role="img" aria-label="npm run build makes dist"><rect class="bx-warn" x="6" y="8" width="196" height="150" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="16" y="30" style="font-size:15px">stage 1: build</text><text class="t-m" x="16" y="54" style="font-size:14px">node:24-alpine</text><text class="t-m" x="16" y="82" style="font-size:14px">node_modules/</text><text class="t-m" x="16" y="106" style="font-size:14px">src/</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="16" y="116" width="80" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="56" y="137.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">dist/</text><rect class="bx-dark" x="6" y="170" width="408" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="196" style="font-size:15px">RUN npm install &amp;&amp; npm run build</text></svg>`],
 ['A second <b>FROM</b> starts a brand-new, tiny image: nginx on Alpine. It knows nothing about stage 1.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 220" role="img" aria-label="Stage 2 starts from nginx alpine"><rect class="bx-warn" x="6" y="8" width="196" height="150" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="16" y="30" style="font-size:15px">stage 1: build</text><text class="t-m" x="16" y="54" style="font-size:14px">node:24-alpine</text><text class="t-m" x="16" y="82" style="font-size:14px">node_modules/</text><text class="t-m" x="16" y="106" style="font-size:14px">src/</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="16" y="116" width="80" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="56" y="137.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">dist/</text><rect class="bx" x="218" y="8" width="196" height="150" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="228" y="30" style="font-size:15px">stage 2: ship</text><text class="t-m" x="228" y="54" style="font-size:14px">nginx:alpine</text><text class="t-m" x="228" y="82" style="font-size:14px">/usr/share/</text><text class="t-m" x="228" y="102" style="font-size:14px">nginx/html</text><rect class="bx-dark" x="6" y="170" width="408" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="196" style="font-size:15px">FROM nginx:alpine</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>COPY --from=build</b> reaches back into stage 1 and copies just the dist folder into nginx\'s web folder.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 220" role="img" aria-label="dist is copied into stage 2"><rect class="bx-warn" x="6" y="8" width="196" height="150" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="16" y="30" style="font-size:15px">stage 1: build</text><text class="t-m" x="16" y="54" style="font-size:14px">node:24-alpine</text><text class="t-m" x="16" y="82" style="font-size:14px">node_modules/</text><text class="t-m" x="16" y="106" style="font-size:14px">src/</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="16" y="116" width="80" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="56" y="137.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">dist/</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="218" y="8" width="196" height="150" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="228" y="30" style="font-size:15px">stage 2: ship</text><text class="t-m" x="228" y="54" style="font-size:14px">nginx:alpine</text><text class="t-m" x="228" y="82" style="font-size:14px">/usr/share/</text><text class="t-m" x="228" y="102" style="font-size:14px">nginx/html</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="316" y="116" width="80" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="356" y="137.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">dist/</text><path class="ln-ok" d="M96 132H308"/><polygon class="ah-ok" points="306,125 306,139 316,132"/><rect class="bx-dark" x="6" y="170" width="408" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="196" style="font-size:15px">COPY --from=build /app/dist ...</text></svg>`],
 ['Only the <b>last</b> stage becomes the image. Node, npm and node_modules stay behind in the workshop.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 220" role="img" aria-label="Only stage 2 is kept"><rect class="ln-d" x="6" y="8" width="196" height="150" rx="8"/><text class="t-b t-dim" x="104" y="90" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:16px">thrown away</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="218" y="8" width="196" height="150" rx="8"/><text class="t-b" x="228" y="30" style="font-size:15px">stage 2: ship</text><text class="t-m" x="228" y="54" style="font-size:14px">nginx:alpine</text><text class="t-m" x="228" y="82" style="font-size:14px">/usr/share/</text><text class="t-m" x="228" y="102" style="font-size:14px">nginx/html</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="316" y="116" width="80" height="32" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="356" y="137.25" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:15px;font-weight:700">dist/</text><rect class="bx-dark" x="6" y="170" width="408" height="40" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="196" style="font-size:15px">image = stage 2 only: small</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.ok('AS build','Name your stages; --from=0 also works but is harder to read'),V.no('COPY --from=build . .','Copying everything brings node_modules along and undoes the point'),
 V.ok('docker images','Compare the SIZE column of site:fat and site:slim'))}
${V.hook(`Build fat, ship thin.`)}
`)}

${V.card(2,'Registries and tags','give every release a name and a number',`
<figure class="fig"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 170" role="img" aria-label="Your laptop pushes you/site:1.0 to a registry, which keeps versions 1.0 and 1.1; a server pulls the version it needs"><rect class="bx-a" x="6" y="40" width="100" height="96" rx="8"/>${V.ic('laptop',26,48,60,'ic-a')}<text class="t" x="56" y="126" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">laptop</text><path class="ln-a" d="M106 70H142"/><polygon class="ah-a" points="140,63 140,77 150,70"/><text class="t-m t-a" x="128" y="60" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">push</text><rect class="bx-info" x="150" y="10" width="120" height="150" rx="8"/>${V.ic('cloud',186,14,48,'ic-info')}<text class="t-b" x="210" y="80" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">registry</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="155" y="92" width="110" height="26" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="210" y="109.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">you/site:1.0</text><rect class="bx" x="155" y="124" width="110" height="26" rx="8"/><text class="t-m" x="210" y="141.9" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">you/site:1.1</text><path class="ln-ok" d="M270 105H306"/><polygon class="ah-ok" points="304,98 304,112 314,105"/><text class="t-m t-ok" x="292" y="95" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">pull</text><rect class="bx-ok" x="314" y="40" width="100" height="96" rx="8"/>${V.ic('server',334,48,60,'ic-ok')}<text class="t" x="364" y="126" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:14px">server</text></svg><figcaption>A registry is a shared shelf of images. You push a version up once; any server or CI pipeline pulls exactly that version down.</figcaption></figure>
${V.like(`<p>A library catalogue. The registry is the library, your username is your shelf, the repository is the book title and the tag is the edition. "you/site, edition 1.0" always means the same book.</p>`)}
${V.anat([[1,'docker.io/'],[2,'you'],'/',[3,'site'],':',[4,'1.0']],[
 '<b>Registry.</b> Where the image lives. Docker Hub (docker.io) is the default, so you can leave it out. Others include ghcr.io for GitHub.',
 '<b>Namespace.</b> Your username or organisation. Pushing needs it: you can\'t push to the official library.',
 '<b>Repository.</b> The image name. Lower case.',
 '<b>Tag.</b> The version. Change it for every release.'])}
${V.steps([
 ['Log in to the registry once. Docker remembers the login.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 156" role="img" aria-label="docker login succeeds"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="144" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ docker login</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">Username: you</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">Password:</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">Login Succeeded</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>docker tag</b> adds a second name to the same image. Nothing is copied: both names show the same IMAGE ID.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 186" role="img" aria-label="docker tag adds a name, same ID"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="174" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ docker tag site:slim you/site:1.0</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ docker images</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">REPOSITORY  TAG   IMAGE ID</text><text class="t-term" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">site        slim  4c1e9a2b7d10</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="156" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">you/site    1.0   4c1e9a2b7d10</text></svg>`],
 ['<b>docker push</b> uploads the layers to your account. Layers the registry already has (like nginx\'s) are skipped.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 156" role="img" aria-label="docker push uploads the image"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="144" rx="8"/><text class="t-term" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">$ docker push you/site:1.0</text><text class="t-term t-dim" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">... Mounted from library/nginx</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">... Pushed</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="126" style="font-size:15px;white-space:pre">1.0: digest: sha256:9b0f... size: 1570</text></svg>`],
 ['Now any server can run exactly this version with one line. That is how deployments get the image.',`<svg viewBox="0 0 420 156" role="img" aria-label="a server pulls the image"><rect class="bx-dark" x="4" y="6" width="412" height="144" rx="8"/><text class="t-term t-a" x="16" y="36" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">deploy@web1:~$ docker pull you/site:1.0</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="66" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">Status: Downloaded newer image for</text><text class="t-term t-ok" x="16" y="96" style="font-size:14px;white-space:pre">  you/site:1.0</text></svg>`]])}
${V.rules(V.rh('Rules'),
 V.no('docker push site:slim','No username: "requested access to the resource is denied"'),V.ok('docker push you/site:1.0','Namespace, name and tag'),
 V.no('COPY .env into an image','Anyone who pulls the image gets your secrets'),
 V.rh('Conventions'),V.ok(':1.0, :1.1, :1.2','A new tag per release, so you can roll back'),V.no(':latest in production','You can\'t tell which version is actually running'))}
${V.build(`<ol><li>Build the existing single-stage Dockerfile as <code>site:fat</code>.</li><li>Rewrite it as two stages: Node builds, nginx:alpine ships the dist folder.</li><li>Build it as <code>site:slim</code> and compare sizes.</li><li>Run the slim image with port 8080 published and curl it.</li><li>Log in, tag it with your username and a version, and push it.</li></ol>`)}
${V.hook(`registry/user/name:tag. Log in, tag, push. Never ship <code>:latest</code> alone.`)}
`)}

<div class="try"><b>Try it in your head</b>1. In a multi-stage build, which stage becomes the image? <i>The last one.</i> 2. Does <code>docker tag</code> make a copy? <i>No, it adds another name for the same image.</i> 3. Why version tags instead of :latest? <i>You always know what runs, and you can roll back.</i></div>
`);

